    {
      "id": "clm_01M4VQCQKXYQFEDJP4ZKP65C5C",
      "statement": "The \"Artaxerxes\" of Ezra 7 is Artaxerxes I, so that Ezra came to Jerusalem in 458 BC, before Nehemiah.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Ezra.7.7-Ezra.7.8",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Keil, Ryle and Yamauchi (via Guzik) take the king as Artaxerxes I and date the journey to 458. Batten places Ezra after Nehemiah, in the early fourth century (under Artaxerxes II), regarding the \"seventh year\" as the Chronicler's unreliable dating, though he declines Kosters's precise 398. Josephus names Xerxes (seventh year, c. 479/478). The chronology on this record encodes the Artaxerxes I reading (constraint assumption); the alternatives are not modelled.",
